{"name":"Voltage","hex":"#3b4956","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"voltage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The difference in electrostatic potential between two points in space, especially between live and neutral conductors or the earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voltage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Voltage","blocks":[{"text":"Voltage, also known as (electrical) potential difference, electric pressure, or electric tension, is the difference in electric potential between two points. In a static electric field, it corresponds to the work needed per unit of charge to move a positive test charge from the first point to the second point. In the International System of Units (SI), the derived unit for voltage is the volt (V)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/AA_AAA_AAAA_A23_battery_comparison-1.jpg/330px-AA_AAA_AAAA_A23_battery_comparison-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voltage","wikidata":"Q25428"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Opfindelsernes_bog3_fig282.png/500px-Opfindelsernes_bog3_fig282.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Opfindelsernes_bog3_fig282.png/1280px-Opfindelsernes_bog3_fig282.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Opfindelsernes_bog3_fig282.png/500px-Opfindelsernes_bog3_fig282.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The electric field around the rod exerts a force on the charged pith ball, in an electroscope","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOpfindelsernes_bog3_fig282.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/US_Navy_110315-N-0278E-002_High-voltage_electr